SUMMARY:CCS $50\,000 Riftbound Invitational
DTSTAMP:20260806T111137Z
DTSTART:20261106T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:CCS $50\,000 Riftbound Invitational – 2026 Series Overview\nThe
	 CCS $50\,000 Riftbound Invitational is a year-long competitive circuit fo
	r Riftbound players. \nThe season concludes on November 6–8\, 2026 in Hous
	ton\, Texas\, with a $50\,000 Invite-Only Championship featuring 128 of th
	e best players in the game. \nGo to the Topdeck Invitational Page \n\nHow 
	to Qualify for the $50\,000 Invitational\n3 Ways to Qualify (128 Total Spo
	ts)\n1. Auto-Qualify – Top 8 from each $25K Main Event (6 events) \nTotal 
	Spots: 48 \n2. Points Leaderboard – Top performers across all events \nTot
	al Spots: 64 \n3. LCQ Winners – Winner of each Last Chance Qualifier (16 e
	vents) \nTotal Spots: 16 \nIf a player qualifies through multiple methods\
	, leaderboard spots roll down to the next eligible player. \n\nBonus for t
	he Most Consistent Players\nThe Top 8 players on the final Points Leaderbo
	ard earn a Round 1 Bye at the Invitational. \n\nMain Qualifier Weekends – 
	Structure & Prizes\nEach of the 6 qualifier weekends includes: \nSaturday 
	– $25\,000 Main Event\n\nFormat: Standard\nSwiss + Top Cut\nTop 8 auto-qua
	lify\nTop 128 placements earn leaderboard points\n\nSunday – $5\,000 Side 
	Event\n\nOne-day event\nTop 8 earn 30 leaderboard points\nNo auto-invite\n
	\n\nLeaderboard Points System\nSaturday $25K Main Events (Top 128 Earn Poi
	nts)\n1st — 100 \n2nd — 80 \n3rd–4th — 65 \n5th–8th — 50 \n9th–16th — 35 \
	n17th–32nd — 20 \n33rd–64th — 10 \n65th–128th — 5 \nTotal Points per Main 
	Event: 1\,750 \nTotal Across All 6: 10\,500 \nSunday $5K Side Events — Poi
	nts\nTop 8 — 30 points each \n\nLast Chance Qualifiers (LCQs)\n\n16 total 
	events\nWinner of each LCQ earns an automatic invite\nOpen entry — no prio
	r points required\n\n\n📍 Main Qualifier Tournament Weekends (6 Total)\nAll
	 dates and locations as scheduled for the 2026 CCS $50\,000 Riftbound Invi
	tational season. \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #1\nJanuary 31 – February 1\, 2026 
	\n📍 Houston\, Texas \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSunday – $5\,000 S
	ide Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗 https://topdeck.gg/event/25000-hou
	ston-invitational-qualifier-1 \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #2\nMarch 13–15\, 2026
	 \n📍 Houston\, Texas \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSunday – $5\,000 
	Side Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗  https://topdeck.gg/event/25000-h
	ouston-invitational-qualifier-2 \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #3\nMay 23–24\, 2026
	 \n📍 Atlanta\, Georgia \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSunday – $5\,00
	0 Side Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗 https://topdeck.gg/event/25000-
	houston-invitational-qualifier-3 \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #4\nJuly 18–19\, 20
	26 \n📍 Atlanta\, Georgia \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSunday – $5\,
	000 Side Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗 https://topdeck.gg/event/2500
	0-atlanta-invitational-qualifier-4 \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #5\nSeptember 19–
	20\, 2026 \n📍 Houston\, Texas \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSunday –
	 $5\,000 Side Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗 https://topdeck.gg/event
	/25000-houston-invitational-qualifier-5 \n🗓️ Qualifier Weekend #6\nOctober 
	10-11\, 2026 \n📍 Atlanta\, Georgia \n\nSaturday – $25\,000 Main Event\nSun
	day – $5\,000 Side Event (Top 8 earn 30 pts each)\n\n🔗 Rhttps://topdeck.gg
	/event/25000-atlanta-invitational-qualifier-6 \n \n\nCCS $50\,000 Riftboun
	d Invitational Championship Weekend\nNovember 6–8\, 2026 \n📍 Houston\, Tex
	as \n128 players compete for $50\,000 and the title of CCS Riftbound Champ
	ion.\n\nhttps://ccs-houston.com/events/ccs-50000-riftbound-invitational/\n
	\nFrom CCS Houston
URL:https://ccs-houston.com/events/ccs-50000-riftbound-invitational/
